<title>ITALY: TABLE-Luxottica Q2 ADS $0.87 vs $0.78.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Luxottica Q2 ADS $0.87 vs $0.78.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second quarter and first six months 1997 (figures are in billion lire unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>					  1997		1996</p>
<p>    Q2 ADS			    $0.87     vs    $0.78</p>
<p>    H1 ADS			    $1.72     vs    $1.56</p>
<p>    H1 group net profit	   128.7     vs    109.4</p>
<p>	 group turnover	   1,385.3     vs  1,271.2</p>
<p>					  1997		1996</p>
<p>    H1 cons net margin	     9.3 pct vs	8.6 pct</p>
<p>	 earnings per ADS	 2,964 lire vs   2,434 lire</p>
<p>	 cons gross profit     1,002.5     vs    896.4</p>
<p>	 gross margin		 72.4 pct vs     70.4 pct</p>
<p>	 operating income	  230.9     vs   (up 13.0 pct)</p>
<p>	 net financial expenses/</p>
<p>	 net sales		     3.3 pct vs	4.3 pct</p>
<p>    Q2 net sales		   699.6     vs    626.2</p>
<p>	 net income		   66.0     vs     54.7</p>
<p>Note - Luxottica Group Spa said net outstanding debt stood at $752.1 million at June 30, 1997 from $817.7 million at December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>The company said it considered financial results denomiated in lire a more accurate gauge of its operating performance and said results in dollars were converted at the H1 1997 average of $1=1,664.3 lire vs $1=1,564.5 for H1 1996.</p>
<p>Conversion for Q2 1997 was $1=1,690.1 vs Q2 1996 $1=1,556.1.</p>
<p>Luxottica said in a statement that in the first half of 1997 it sold 10.1 million frames and added in order to expand its distribution network it would open a 100 percent controlled subsidiary in South Africa in the next few months.</p>
<p>Optical chain LensCrafters' first half sales rose 9.0 percent to $500.6 million.</p>
